WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.520
- All right, before we go,
let me serve up one last story

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:03.670
that might bring you some joy.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:04.691
This is "What I'm Liking."

00:00:04.691 --> 00:00:05.607
(upbeat music)

00:00:05.607 --> 00:00:08.310
(audience cheers)

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:09.910
A woman in Australia named Ingrid

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:11.500
is stepping up to rehabilitate

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:13.900
a neighborhood thief, even inviting him

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:15.910
to live in her home for good.

00:00:15.910 --> 00:00:17.545
Here's the criminal's mugshot.

00:00:17.545 --> 00:00:19.050
(audience laughs)

00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:19.920
Yup.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:22.370
Pirate Kitty Kylo as he's known

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.670
spent months stealing hundreds of items,

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:27.920
hundreds, from neighbors'
porches and yards.

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.536
Everything from gloves to shoes to toys.

00:00:30.536 --> 00:00:31.520
(laughs) It's awesome.

00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:34.420
His original owners posted
the goods on social media

00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:36.060
for people to reclaim,

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:38.040
and while some thought it was adorable,

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:40.150
others not so much because they're no fun

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:40.983
'cause it's funny.

00:00:40.983 --> 00:00:42.550
(audience laughs)

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:43.660
What's happening in your world

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.840
that you can't find that funny?

00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:47.280
Anyway, they knew Pirate
Kitty needed some help,

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.680
so that's where Ingrid stepped in.

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:52.610
So we have her on the line
along with Pirate Kitty himself.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:53.914
What's up, Ingrid?

00:00:53.914 --> 00:00:56.003
(audience cheers)

00:00:56.003 --> 00:00:56.970
- Hi, Kelly.

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:58.170
Hi, everybody.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.800
- Oh my god, I love Pirate Kitty.

00:00:59.800 --> 00:01:03.000
So explain how you ended up
taking care of Pirate Kitty.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.049
- Well, not everybody
loves Pirate, you see.

00:01:06.049 --> 00:01:07.890
And his owners were
getting a lot of complaints

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:11.840
to local council and they
had threats against him,

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.440
and so they decided that the
best thing that they could do

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.880
was to try and rehome him.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.748
And that's how he came to me.

00:01:17.748 --> 00:01:20.960
And so I volunteered to put
him into witness protection,

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.520
which is where you change his name,

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.870
you change his location, and help him

00:01:24.870 --> 00:01:28.140
to become a quiet indoor kitty,

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:29.710
but the community was having none of it.

00:01:29.710 --> 00:01:32.960
They just wanted to know where
he was, what he was doing,

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:36.230
and so I started posting
his information on socials.

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:37.330
- So, here is my thing.

00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:38.830
If we could go back to that picture

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:40.419
with all that crap on that table.

00:01:40.419 --> 00:01:41.622
(audience laughs)

00:01:41.622 --> 00:01:44.220
Why are all these people not thanking him

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:45.830
for his service like a public service?

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.939
All this crap is just laying
out in peoples' yards?

00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:49.440
(audience laughs)

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.360
Like I have a problem with
these people, not this cat.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:56.370
This cat is trying to help us be clean.

00:01:56.370 --> 00:01:57.203
That is just wrong.

00:01:57.203 --> 00:01:58.040
Is he still a thief?

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.050
Does he steal stuff in your house?

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:01.940
- He definitely still is a thief.

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.590
Now, he's a fully indoor kitty

00:02:03.590 --> 00:02:06.580
and his routine is the second
that the lights go out,

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:08.380
whatever is not nailed down in the house

00:02:08.380 --> 00:02:11.100
gets stolen and taken up to the landing

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.890
outside our bedrooms,
which we call loot landing.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:15.140
And every night we come out,

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:16.570
and there's more things out there.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.090
There's toys, swishy sticks,

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:20.800
his favorite is a Elf on the Shelf,

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:22.380
and every morning when we get out of bed,

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.370
he's sitting there waiting for his photo

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.739
'cause he's so proud of what he's done.

00:02:26.739 --> 00:02:28.940
My only regret, though,

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.310
is I bought him a very, very
noisy toy called a Floppy Fish,

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:34.410
which is one of those
battery operated fish

00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:35.880
that jump up and down.

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:39.110
Great, except at 2:00
am it's extremely noisy,

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:41.070
but he's happy, and
that's all that matters.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:42.380
- Yeah, my poor dog.

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.770
He has never had a noisy toy.

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:47.730
Yeah, and he shall never
'cause I don't wanna hear it

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:48.980
in my house (chuckles).

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:51.270
I'm like, "I'll play fetch
with you, I'll love on you,

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:52.950
you are not getting a noisy toy."

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.390
Thank you so much, Ingrid.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:55.870
I love that he's such a helper

00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.160
and he's trying to clean
up the neighborhood

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.240
is what he was doing.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:00.484
I'm liking your post right now, all right?

00:03:00.484 --> 00:03:02.890
(audience applauds)

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:04.010
And that's not all, ma'am,

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.760
our season long partner,
Pilot Pin makers of G2,

00:03:06.760 --> 00:03:08.410
the go-to pin of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:10.670
wanna honor ultimate
overachievers just like you

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:12.980
and a special park kitty
trying to clean up the world,

00:03:12.980 --> 00:03:15.956
so they're gonna be writing
you a check for $1,000.

00:03:15.956 --> 00:03:16.789
(audience applauds)

00:03:16.789 --> 00:03:17.789
- Thank you.

00:03:18.777 --> 00:03:19.640
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:20.940
Thank you so much, Ingrid!

